# API base URL is a secret-in-repo

This repo is public. Do **not** put the live API hostname in committed files.

## Must

- Read the host only via `ApiConfig` (`lib/data/api/api_config.dart`).
- Store the real value in local `.env` (`API_BASE_URL`, no trailing slash).
- Run / build with `--dart-define-from-file=.env`.
- Keep `.env` gitignored. Commit `.env.example` with an empty value.

## Must not

- Hardcode `https://…` API hosts in Dart, tests, README, PROJECT.md, CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or rules.
- Describe APIs, servers, hosts, or endpoints in any `*.md` file (this repo is public).
- Commit `.env`, `api.md` dumps, or cURL samples that include the real host.
- Bundle `.env` as a Flutter asset (`flutter_dotenv` in `pubspec` assets).
- Print `ApiConfig.baseUrl` in logs, crash reports, or UI.

## Example

```dart
// BAD
final uri = Uri.parse('https://example-live-host/api/your_routine');

// GOOD
final uri = ApiConfig.uri('/api/your_end_point');
```

```bash
flutter run --dart-define-from-file=.env
flutter test --dart-define-from-file=.env
```
